 r←GetMetaDescription description
⍝ Returns the <meta name="description"> tag for a package page, ready to be passed to
⍝ `HtmlHeader` as ⍵, or '' when there is nothing to say.
⍝ It travels in ⍵ rather than in a new item of ⍺ because ⍵ is precisely what ⍵ is for:
⍝ whatever else belongs in the head of this particular page.
⍝ Search engines often write their own snippet rather than use this, but a description
⍝ written by the package's author beats anything that could be invented here, and it is the
⍝ text a reader sees under the link before deciding whether to follow it.
 r←''
 :If 0<≢description
     r←⊂'<meta name="description" content="',(EscapeAttributeValue description),'">'
 :EndIf
